:: Attack [Outcome] {"position":"500,500","size":"100,100"}
You signal your squad to attack the monster. With a loud battle scream all of you charge foward towards the monster.

With a deep roar the monster turns to look at the squad, charging at them.

Bullets fly towards the monster, piercing through its skin. The monster uses the claws on its hand to cause wounds on your team, catches one of your teammates with his huge hand and slams him into the ground. It lowers its head to bite your teammate head off.

With his remaining strength, your teammate grabs his combat knife and stabs the monster in the eye. The monster whines in pain and retreats, collapsing in the grass agonizingly.

[[You stare at the monster]]


:: Climb the tree [Main-Event] {"position":"1100,700","size":"100,100"}
You climb the tree with ease, reaching a high branch and observe your surroundings. You can see in the distance a bright light. Could that be the answer to close the portals?

You look around to find the best path to arrive there. You can see three posible safe paths:

The right path is between rocks that give cover, to the left is the forest, and in the middle is the clear zone. All paths lead to the bright light.

What path will you take?

[[Go right]]
[[Go left]]
[[Go middle]]


:: Destroy it [Ending] {"position":"1700,700","size":"100,100"}
With rage you grab and destroy it, one last portal shows up in front of your team. You can see the real world through it, the world behind you is collapsing more and more every second you stay there.

You guide your team through the portal, appearing in the same place you entered the portal.

You see the leaders of the operation waiting for the report, portal closing behind you.

You give the news of the loss of 3 members with a heavy heart. The mission might be succesful but it left you feeling guilt over their deaths.

(text-colour:red)[''THE END'']


:: Flee [Outcome] {"position":"500,900","size":"100,100"}
You signal your squad to retreat back to the portal, the monster looks way too powerful to combat it.

You and your team slowly walk towards the portal, when suddenly you hear the snap of a branch close to you, you turn and see one of your teammates stepped on a broken branch.

Before you can think about anything else the monster sprints towards you all, attacking the closest person to it.

The monsters assault is overwhelming. In a last minute effort, you throw your knife aiming at the stomach, hitting the target and making the monster retreat.

The monster collapses, painful whines coming out of its mouth.

[[You stare at the monster]]


:: Go inside the portal [Main-Event] {"position":"300,700","size":"100,100"}
You walk inside the portal, your team is not so far behind. The world before your eyes is full of blue plants, the sky color a nauseous green. This place makes you question everything you've learned about the universe.

You're taken away from your thoughts when one of your teammates points at a nearby clear.

In the middle of it, you see a monster, it is sniffing around like it was looking for something.

You have 3 options. What will you do?

[[Attack]]
[[Hide]]
[[Flee]]


:: Go left [Outcome] {"position":"1300,500","size":"100,100"}
You climb down from the tree, once you are completely down you guide your group to the forest.

You see animal life, "normal" looking animals.

Your team spots deer nearby. They're staring at your team, getting closer slowly, until suddenly their antlers stab 3 of your squad, leaving them motionless on the antlers.

The rest of your team shoots at the deer, killing them. You can't do anything than show grief in your face.

[[Keep going]] 


:: Go middle [Outcome] {"position":"1300,700","size":"100,100"}
You climb down from the tree, once you are completely down you guide your group foward to the clearing, nothing can surprise you all there.

You and your squad walk for a while, seeing the light closer and closer. Before arriving, a monster double the size of the other one attacks from the air, killing one of your teammates instantly.

The rest shoot the monster, it takes another one of the team and drops it from a high altitude, aiming for another teammate.

You know this battle can't be won, so you yell at your squad to flee.

The monster attacks the 3rd teammate, killing eat and eating it. You take the opportunity and leave the place.

[[Keep going]] 



:: Go right [Outcome] {"position":"1300,900","size":"100,100"}
You climb down from the tree, once you are completely down you guide your group to the right between the rocks, the cover they give giving you all a sense of safety.

In the middle of the travel you feel the land shake, you look up and see rocks falling in your direction.

You warn your squad but it's too late. Three of your squad got squished under a rock, the rest taking cover behind a nearby big rock. You join them.

Once the rocks stop falling, you come out of cover, grief showing on your face. There's no way back at this point.

[[Keep going]] 



:: Hide [Outcome] {"position":"500,700","size":"100,100"}
You look at the monster and decided it's too dangerous to fight it.

You signal your team to hide in some nearby bushes, waiting for the monster to eventually leave the zone.

The monster roams the clearing, sniffing, until it walks away and disappears toward some bushes.

You and your team relax, when suddenly one of the teammates is attacked in the back, being thrown a couple of meters towards the clearing leaving him with a deep wound. You hear a roar behind you, the monster attacked by surprise.

Your team shoots directly at the monster, dodging its attacks as best as they can.

You find an old wound on the monsters chest and charge towards it, grabing the knife on your belt and stabbing it directly on the old wound.

The monster whines in pain and retreats, collapsing in the grass agonizingly.

[[You stare at the monster]]


:: Introduction [Start] {"position":"100,700","size":"100,100"}
The world has changed. After the elite of the world experimented with multiverse, Exploration Portals have been showing up all over the world. Monsters that people had nightmares about now roaming freely in our land.

You've been chosen to command a task force with 10 other strong individuals. Your objective is to explore inside these portals to find a way to stop this madness.

You and your team are equipped and ready to explore a nearby portal. 

The decisions you take will have consequences...

[[Go inside the portal]]


:: Keep going [Main-Event] {"position":"1500,700","size":"100,100"}
Your squad is feeling hopeless, scared that they will be the next ones to die.

It doesn't take much longer to arrive at the light. You see the original device that opened the first portal floating and emitting light.

[[Destroy it]] 


:: Kill it [Outcome] {"position":"900,600","size":"100,100"}
Without thinking twice you approach the monster, using a knife your squad gave you and cut the monsters throat open in a single movement.

The monster whines in pain for a second before finally dying, its body collapsing completely.

Your team regroups, treating the wounds. Once everyone is back on their feet you look around, finding a tree tall enough to help you see around if you climb it.

[[Climb the tree]]


:: Leave it agonizing [Outcome] {"position":"900,800","size":"100,100"}
You stare at the monster with hate, killing it is a mercy the monster doesn't deserve. Without thinking it twice you leave the monster agonizing, hoping that it dies slowly and in pain.

You look at your squad regrouping and treating their wounds. Once everyone is back on their feet you look around, the monsters painful whines in the background, stopping when you see a tree tall enough to help you see around.

[[Climb the tree]] 


:: You stare at the monster [Main-Event] {"position":"700,700","size":"100,100"}
The tension starts to fade away, you and your team regroup to treat wounds.

The monster keeps whining in the background, slowly bleeding out. You are staring at it since the battle finished, thinking on what to do next.

Would you end its suffering and kill it in an act of mercy, or leave it to agonize until it dies?

[[Kill it]]
[[Leave it agonizing]]

